  "final_text": "All four steps are done.\n\n1. **Data view:** \"Kibana Sample Data Flights\" has 33 fields, including `Carrier`, `Cancelled` and `timestamp`. Its time field is `timestamp`.\n2. **Dashboard:** \"S4-6cc46566 Flights\" has two panels. One is a line chart of flights over time. The other is a bar chart of flights by carrier. I first gave the carrier panel the title \"Flights by carrier two\" by mistake, and step 4 corrected it.\n3. **Alert rule:** \"S4-6cc46566 Cancelled flights\" is an `.es-query` rule on `kibana_sample_data_flights`. It runs every minute and fires when more than 10 documents with `Cancelled: true` arrive in a 5-minute window. It was created disabled, so I enabled it.\n4. **Edits and read-back:** I renamed the carrier panel to \"Flights by carrier\". Reading the rule back shows `enabled: true` and status `ok`.\n\nTIME_FIELD: timestamp\nRULE_ENABLED: yes",
